---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Whetstone Creator — stress-test your writing | The Whetstone"
  description="The same engine that powers Devil's Advocate, pointed at your draft. Argument structure, reasoning patterns, and the counterarguments your piece doesn't engage with."
  canonicalPath="/creator"
>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-20 pb-16">

    <nav class="mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-xs text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-600 transition-colors">← The Whetstone</a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-amber-600 uppercase mb-3">For creators</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-4">
        Whetstone Creator
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
        The same engine that powers Devil's Advocate, pointed at your draft. Argument structure,
        reasoning patterns, citation audit, the strongest opposing case, and the counterarguments
        your piece doesn't engage with.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <a
        href="/creator/studio"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 bg-amber-500 text-white text-sm font-medium rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-600 transition-colors"
      >
        Try the Studio
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
        </svg>
      </a>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-gray-400">Free during early access — design partners get priority feedback.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- What the studio does -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-gray-400 uppercase mb-6">What the studio returns</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700">
        <li class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900">Argument Structure.</strong> The main claim, the evidence offered in support, and the hidden assumptions connecting them — plus the single weakest point in the chain.
        </li>
        <li class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900">Reasoning Patterns.</strong> High-confidence only — false positives at the pre-publish moment are trust-killing. The tool says nothing when it is uncertain.
        </li>
        <li class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900">Citation audit.</strong> Every factual claim mapped as cited well, cited weakly (source doesn't quite say that), or uncited.
        </li>
        <li class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900">Steelman.</strong> The strongest version of the opposing view to what the draft argues, with sources. Useful precisely because it isn't a caricature.
        </li>
        <li class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900">Blind-spot counterarguments.</strong> The two or three strongest objections the piece doesn't address — so you can engage them before your readers do.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Persona cards -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-gray-400 uppercase mb-6">Who it serves</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100 bg-white">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Students</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Thesis structure, evidence quality, counterargument handling, citation integrity aligned
            to MLA / APA / Chicago. The question is "is your argument sound?" — not "did you write this?"
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100 bg-white">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Journalists</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Source verification, counterargument coverage, warrant exposure, charitable-framing check.
            Available for self-adoption by freelancers or as multi-seat for small investigative newsrooms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100 bg-white">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">YouTubers</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Per-segment audit keyed to script paragraphs, claim-density chart, and a downloadable
            critique memo for your researcher or editor. For essay and long-form analysis channels.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100 bg-white">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Substackers</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Reader-framing check, steelman mode, source verification against your draft, and a
            pre-publish audit flow before you send to your list.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100 bg-white sm:col-span-2">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Newsrooms <span class="font-normal text-gray-400">— enquire</span></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Multi-author review, editorial workflow integration, CMS hooks. Design partner conversations
            open. <a href="mailto:daniel.livingstone44@gmail.com" class="text-amber-600 hover:text-amber-800 underline underline-offset-2">Get in touch →</a>
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pricing teaser -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-gray-400 uppercase mb-6">Indicative pricing</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-5">Finalising with design partners — all figures illustrative.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100">
          <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-0.5">Creator Solo</div>
          <div class="text-lg font-serif text-gray-700 mb-2">$20–30 <span class="text-sm font-sans font-normal text-gray-400">/mo</span></div>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Students, indie Substackers, solo YouTubers, freelance journalists.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100">
          <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-0.5">Creator Studio</div>
          <div class="text-lg font-serif text-gray-700 mb-2">$80–120 <span class="text-sm font-sans font-normal text-gray-400">/mo</span></div>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Multi-seat: writer + researcher, mid-tier YouTube channels, small podcast teams.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100">
          <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-0.5">Creator Team</div>
          <div class="text-lg font-serif text-gray-700 mb-2">$250–400 <span class="text-sm font-sans font-normal text-gray-400">/mo</span></div>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">10 seats, admin dashboard, API access, heavier writing operations.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-100">
          <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-0.5">Newsroom</div>
          <div class="text-lg font-serif text-gray-700 mb-2">Custom</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Small investigative newsrooms, nonprofit journalism, publishing organisations.</div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Base>
